body:
**MMR-33 handoff: entities, gates, ports, siege geometry**

All MMR-33 positions are staged (`pendingEngineValidation`):
- the centre is the MMR-28 point;
- the gate is the centre (town and castle gates are written explicitly);
- town ports are the MMR-28 sea point, within the installed port-gate maximum 10.97 plus one cell of the staged gate. 19 of the 30 ports are farther than the installed port-centre maximum (6.96) until gates are placed;
- harbour-village ports are at the harbour-cell centre.

**Entities.** Each intent carries `mapPrefab`: the prototype's vanilla Main_map `old_prefab_name`. Towns have none, because the vanilla map does not place them as prefabs. The installed `MapScene.AddNewEntityToMapScene` instantiates a prefab named after the settlement id. A generated id has no such prefab, which caused the run 36452 NRE in `SettlementVisual.OnStartup`. The fixture-only shim is `DiagnosticMapScene.AddNewEntityToMapScene` (FixturePrefabs).

**Siege positions** are not written. `Town.Deserialize` leaves the besieger camp positions at identity, and `SettlementVisual.OnStartup` fills siege-engine frames from the map entity's children. They are MMR-40's.

The in-game fixtures (run 37100) verify that the engine reads distinct gates exactly from the XML.
